    a: 'British formal footwear and boots (such as Dr. Martens, Clarks, Loake, Church\'s, and Tricker\'s) are built around UK sizing. In addition to adding 0.5 in length for US men\'s sizing, pay attention to width fittings: standard British \'F\' fitting is comparable to American \'D\' (medium), while British \'G\' is a wide fitting equivalent to American \'E/EE\'.'
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I convert UK kids\' shoe sizes to US sizing?',
    a: 'In children\'s footwear, British sizes run approximately 0.5 size smaller than US sizes through toddler and little kid stages (e.g., UK 7.5C = US 8C). When transitioning into youth/big kid sizes, British 13.5C converts into US 1Y, and UK 1.5Y corresponds to US 2Y.'
  },
  {
    q: 'How can I measure my foot at home to confirm my exact US and UK size?',
    a: 'Stand barefoot on a blank sheet of paper with your heel against a flat wall. Trace the outline of both feet and measure the distance in centimeters from the wall to the tip of your longest toe. Add 0.5 cm of movement allowance, then reference our conversion table to find your precise UK and US sizes.'
